Each role has multiple built-in implementations chosen by data source and volume.

**Choosing a reader**
- `FlatFileItemReader` — CSV / fixed-width / delimited files
- `JdbcCursorItemReader` — opens a single JDBC cursor for the entire step; great for large datasets but holds a connection open
- `JdbcPagingItemReader` / `JpaPagingItemReader` — offset-based paging; releases the connection between pages; safer for very large datasets but vulnerable to data drift mid-step
- `KafkaItemReader` — consumes from a Kafka topic

**`@StepScope` is non-negotiable for parameterized readers and writers**
- Without `@StepScope`, the reader bean is a singleton — two concurrent job executions share state and corrupt each other
- `@StepScope` defers bean creation until the step starts; `@Value("#{jobParameters['inputFile']}")` resolves at that point

```java
@Bean
@StepScope
public FlatFileItemReader<Order> orderReader(
        @Value("#{jobParameters['inputFile']}") String inputFile) {
    return new FlatFileItemReaderBuilder<Order>()
            .name("orderReader")
            .resource(new FileSystemResource(inputFile))
            .delimited().names("id", "customerId", "amount")
            .targetType(Order.class)
            .saveState(true)
            .build();
}
```

**Composing processors**
- `CompositeItemProcessor` chains multiple processors in order; each receives the output of the previous one
- Cleaner than one monolithic processor with mixed concerns — validate, enrich, transform as separate units

```java
@Bean
public CompositeItemProcessor<Order, Invoice> processor(
        ValidationProcessor validate,
        EnrichmentProcessor enrich,
        TransformProcessor transform) {
    CompositeItemProcessor<Order, Invoice> composite = new CompositeItemProcessor<>();
    composite.setDelegates(List.of(validate, enrich, transform));
    return composite;
}
```

**Choosing a writer**
- `JdbcBatchItemWriter` — uses `PreparedStatement.addBatch()` / `executeBatch()`; one round-trip per chunk
- `JpaItemWriter` — flushes the EntityManager; set `hibernate.jdbc.batch_size=50` and `hibernate.order_inserts=true` to actually batch
- `FlatFileItemWriter` / `StaxEventItemWriter` — for file output
- **Never loop and write one at a time** inside a custom writer — defeats chunk batching

**Testing chunk components**
- `@SpringBatchTest` provides `JobLauncherTestUtils` for end-to-end and `launchStep("name")` for isolated step tests
- `ListItemReader<>(List.of(item1, item2))` is a quick mock reader
- Assert on writer output (in-memory writer) or on database state via TestContainers

`ClassifierCompositeItemWriter` routes each item to **exactly one** writer based on a `Classifier`. Items destined for the same writer are grouped and handed off as a sub-chunk — preserving batching for each destination.

**The Classifier interface**

```java
public interface Classifier<C, T> {
    T classify(C classifiable);
}
```

**Wiring with a classifier function**

```java
@Bean
public ClassifierCompositeItemWriter<User> classifyingWriter(
        JdbcBatchItemWriter<User> validUsersWriter,
        FlatFileItemWriter<User> quarantineWriter) {
    ClassifierCompositeItemWriter<User> writer = new ClassifierCompositeItemWriter<>();
    writer.setClassifier((Classifier<User, ItemWriter<? super User>>) user -> {
        if (user.isValid()) return validUsersWriter;
        return quarantineWriter;
    });
    return writer;
}
```

**`BackToBackPatternClassifier` for pattern-based routing**
- A `BackToBackPatternClassifier` lets you map property values (or regex patterns) to destinations declaratively
- Useful when the routing key is a string code (`region`, `status`)

```java
@Bean
public Classifier<Order, ItemWriter<? super Order>> orderClassifier(
        ItemWriter<Order> usWriter,
        ItemWriter<Order> euWriter,
        ItemWriter<Order> apacWriter) {
    BackToBackPatternClassifier classifier = new BackToBackPatternClassifier();
    PatternMatchingClassifier<String> router = new PatternMatchingClassifier<>(
        Map.of("US*", "us", "EU*", "eu", "APAC*", "apac"));
    SubclassClassifier<Order, String> regionMapper = new SubclassClassifier<>();
    classifier.setRouterDelegate(router);
    classifier.setMatcherMap(Map.of(
        "us", usWriter, "eu", euWriter, "apac", apacWriter));
    return (Classifier) classifier;
}
```

**`ItemStream` propagation requires extra wiring**
- `ClassifierCompositeItemWriter` does NOT automatically propagate `ItemStream` calls
- Wrap it in `CompositeItemStream` or register the delegate writers as separate listeners on the step

```java
@Bean
public Step classifyStep(JobRepository repo, PlatformTransactionManager tx,
                          ItemReader<User> reader,
                          ClassifierCompositeItemWriter<User> writer,
                          FlatFileItemWriter<User> quarantineWriter) {
    return new StepBuilder("classifyStep", repo)
            .<User, User>chunk(500, tx)
            .reader(reader)
            .writer(writer)
            .stream(quarantineWriter)
            .build();
}
```

**Restart and partial-write semantics**
- A failed chunk rolls back ALL sub-chunks across all destinations
- On restart, the entire chunk is re-read and re-classified; idempotency required
- Make sure each destination writer can handle re-writes (UPSERT, idempotency keys)
